    {"id":"visual-stage-n3-001","studyId":"schematic-n3-001","type":"stage-choice","taskCode":"D3A","prompt":"Which stage is this original schematic epoch designed to represent?","options":["W","N1","N2","N3","R"],"answer":"N3","rationale":"This teaching epoch emphasizes sustained slow-wave activity across the EEG montage, with greatest amplitude frontally and related lower-amplitude activity centrally, occipitally, and subtly in the EOG derivations."},
